  "helpSearch": "Search help",
  "helpNoResults": "Nothing found. Try another word.",
  "helpBasicsTitle": "Getting around",
  "helpBasicsBody": "Today shows overdue items first, then what's due or happening today. Upcoming shows the next 7 days, All shows everything as a tree, and Done keeps what you finished, with your weekly count. Drag views and tags in the sidebar to reorder them, and pick the view Wayfinch opens in under Settings › General.\n\nQuick add understands dates, times, tags and priority, in English and French: try \"Lab report Friday 5pm #school !high\" or \"Rapport vendredi 17h #école !haute\".",
  "helpItemsTitle": "Tasks and events",
  "helpItemsBody": "Tasks are due by a date (with an optional time); events run from a start to an end. Click an item to edit it in the panel on the right; changes save as you go. Date and time are set together in one dialog. Deleting shows an Undo for 10 seconds.",
  "helpNestingTitle": "Subtasks",
  "helpNestingBody": "Break things down as far as you like: use \"+ Add subtask\" in the details, or the + on a list row. A few situations ask first: pushing a parent's date when a subtask goes past it, closing open subtasks when a parent is done, and marking a parent done when its last subtask is. Tick \"don't ask again\" to remember your answer; change it anytime in Settings › Prompts.",
  "helpRecurringTitle": "Repeating items",
  "helpRecurringBody": "Use Repeat in the details: daily, weekdays, weekly, every 2 weeks, monthly or yearly. Completing a repeating task creates the next one, with fresh copies of its subtasks. Repeating events roll forward on their own once they end.",
  "helpTagsTitle": "Tags and overdue",
  "helpTagsBody": "Add tags from an item's details. Click a tag in the sidebar to see everything with it. Change a tag's color from its dot in the sidebar, by right-clicking it, or from a tag chip's menu. Overdue items get the automatic \"overdue\" tag, and a banner offers to review them or snooze it until tomorrow.",
  "helpAiTitle": "Using Wayfinch with your AI",
  "helpAiBody": "Export for AI copies your list with the format rules below and your own instructions. Paste it into any AI with a request (\"plan my final project\"), then paste the reply into Import. You'll see what's new, changed and removed before anything happens. Add only adds new items; Replace makes your list match the AI's version (done items are never removed). Your list is backed up first, and you can undo.",
  "helpThemesTitle": "Themes",
  "helpThemesBody": "Settings › Appearance has light, dark or system, five accent colors, and a custom theme builder that warns you when text may be hard to read.",
  "helpPasswordTitle": "Password and recovery code",
  "helpPasswordBody": "A password encrypts your list on this computer. When you set one, you get a recovery code: it can unlock your list if you forget the password. If you lose both, your list can't be recovered. Manage both in Settings › Profile.",
  "helpBackupsTitle": "Backups and undo",
  "helpBackupsBody": "Your list is backed up before every import. Undo the last import from the Import dialog, or restore any of the last 10 backups from Settings › Import history. Restoring backs up your current list first, so you can change your mind."
